 ### Priority
 
@@ -118,15 +118,23 @@ ### Ordering and Fairness
 
 The **next candidate queue** is **deterministic**: same state input → same next ticket, no random draw.
 
+**Implementation (`App\Actions\CallNextTicket`):** candidates are the `waiting` tickets of the given queue only (tickets of other queues are never selected, and an already called ticket is never called again). Full ordering is: higher `priority` first → oldest `issued_at` → lowest `id` as the final tie-break.
+
+**Call modes (`App\Enums\CallMode`):** `any` (full ordering + fairness), `priority_only` (only `priority > 0` tickets, full ordering, fairness ignored) and `normal_only` (only `priority = 0` tickets, oldest first, fairness ignored). When no ticket is eligible for the requested mode, the action throws `App\Exceptions\NoWaitingTicketsException`.
+
+**Fairness rule (any mode only):** a normal ticket may not wait behind more than 3 consecutive priority calls. The action looks at the last 3 tickets **called** in this queue — most recent first by `called_at`, then by `id`: if all three exist, all are priority tickets and at least one normal ticket is waiting, the call is restricted to normal tickets (the oldest normal is called). Calls made in `priority_only`/`normal_only` mode count in that call history; any normal call breaks the streak (the window then contains a normal). If no normal ticket is waiting, priority tickets keep being called.
+
+**Concurrency / exactly-once:** the action runs in a database transaction: it locks the queue row (serializing call-next against queue deactivation and refreshing stale state), picks the ranked candidates, then locks each candidate row and re-checks it is still `waiting` — a concurrent `Ticket::call()` (which does not lock the queue row) is skipped over in favor of the next candidate. Calling from an **inactive queue** is rejected (`App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException`) and changes nothing. On success the ticket's `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` are written (respecting the write-once rule) and the updated ticket is returned.
+
 ### Call Panel (attendant)
 
-Three explicit actions, all deterministic:
+Three explicit actions, all deterministic. Each maps to one `App\Enums\CallMode` passed to `App\Actions\CallNextTicket`:
 
-| Button | Behavior |
-| ----- | ------------- |
-| **Next (most important)** | Calls the next ticket according to full ordering (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness rule). |
-| **Priority** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among priority candidates (includes 80+ per configuration). |
-| **Normal** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among normal candidates. |
+| Button | Mode | Behavior |
+| ----- | ------------- | ------------- |
+| **Next (most important)** | `CallMode::Any` | Calls the next ticket according to full ordering (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness rule). |
+| **Priority** | `CallMode::PriorityOnly` | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among priority candidates (includes 80+ per configuration). |
+| **Normal** | `CallMode::NormalOnly` | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among normal candidates. |
 
 After each call, the ticket leaves the waiting queue and enters the session/display call history.
 
